# Liveness DOUBLE MOVE (`f(!n, !n)`): moving the same place twice in one call.
# Under the ratified pass-order rider (liveness precedes aliasing), the second
# `!n` is caught as a double move — the self-host emits ``n` moved more than once
# (double move)``, NOT the place-overlap diagnostic. This now matches production
# Rust gg + ggdef exactly (E_DoubleMove; their move-tracker preempts
# place-overlap the same way). Before the liveness pass landed, this fired the
# overlap code as a faithful mirror of the FULL D10 rule (reject-with-a-different
# -code beats ACCEPT); the unified check_safety_* walk preempts that arm now.
# Owner ruling "B2 SCOPE + LIVENESS-PASS" 2026-07-14.
struct N:
    Vector[int] data

void f(N !a, N !b):
    pass

void run():
    N n = N(Vector[int]())
    f(!n, !n)

void main():
    run()
